## 4. Adapters at Boundaries

**Trigger**:
- Database/encoding/cache code in domain layer
- Domain types coupled to infrastructure
- Cannot test domain logic without infrastructure
- Violates Dependency Inversion Principle

**Action**:
1. Define **Port** (interface) in domain layer
2. Implement **Adapter** in infrastructure layer
3. Inject adapter through constructor
4. Domain depends only on interface, never on implementation

**Example**:
```go
// Domain Layer (port)
type UserRepository interface {
    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (User, error)
    Save(ctx context.Context, user User) error
}

// Infrastructure Layer (adapter)
type PostgresUserRepository struct {
    db *sql.DB
}

func (r *PostgresUserRepository) FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (User, error) {
    // SQL/scanning details hidden here
    var dto UserDTO
    err := r.db.QueryRowContext(ctx, "SELECT ...").Scan(&dto)
    return dto.ToDomain(), err
}

// Application Layer (composition)
type UserService struct {
    repo UserRepository  // Depends on abstraction
}

func NewUserService(repo UserRepository) *UserService {
    return &UserService{repo: repo}
}
```

